{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/345457-investigator-s-eye-embed","id":345457,"title":"Investigator's Eye Embed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-19T23:32:42-08:00","id":345457,"title":"Investigator's Eye Embed","content":"Salutations and good evening my fellow denizens of the Aether Streams, how does this fine moon lit night fare you? I am Zerik Tigrerious Haruq, in my universe I am the Lord of Chaos, and a rather fine destroyer in my time. If I do say so myself. It has been within the past month I have found I have this thirst for knowledge, and all information that I can find. For this, myself and the great voice in the sky (You all know of it, it reiterates everything you do and say, and those of your team mates... seems pretty stalkerish to me) have created a new Embed, and I wanted to see what you all think of it in the multiverse;<br /> <br /> Investigator's Eye<br /> <br /> Wits+Investigation<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure:<br /> While gathering ambient information from the current scene, all information gleaned is recorded wrong within the Aether Processors, taking a negative to all Investigation rolls equal to the demons primum until the Aether is &quot;cleaned&quot; out.<br /> <br /> Note: Cleaning: Spend Aether equal to your Primum.<br /> <br /> Failure:<br /> The Demon gleans nothing from the current scene.<br /> <br /> Success:<br /> Through just a basic success, the demon is able to glean from the scene small details and make leaps of logic straight from just what he's able to see. From people who are of lower power than he, the demon is able to get basic information about themselves. Also he is able to notice any mental issues the person is exhibiting, as well as physical illnesses that have a noticable effect on the being. With every success, the demon is able to ask the GM one question about the scene that is not viable at first glance, and get detailed info. This embed doesn\u2019t reveal specific, plot-sensitive information that isn\u2019t readily apparent (such as who the perpetrators actually are), but it should provide enough clues in a single glance for the character to develop solid leads that further the story.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success:<br /> As with a success, but the demon is able to notice through Ambient Aether if the scene has been supernaturally altered, or if the person is of a supernatural nature. But it is still unable to tell them what KIND of supernatural they are.<br /> <br /> Note: If the Supernatural is aware of the reading, they are able to spend a point of their power pool to spoof the affect into seeing them as Human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4565,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4565-zeriqharuk","user":"ZeriqHaruk","date":". 12-20-2014, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4565-zeriqharuk","name":"ZeriqHaruk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T20:02:45-08:00","id":347117,"title":"","content":"I honestly, don't understand I think? It seems to be all over the place. When investigating a scene what about it does the character to investigate? It looks like, it reads like the ability discerns information on specific individuals. But then it talks about if the area had been supernaturally altered. Which is the exceptional success result of the embed &quot;synthesis l&quot; dtd pg 138. Asking one question per successes is a little overkill without having any given examples or limitations. This is really more of an exploit anyways. And aether isn't ambient its waste heat. So if that's a big part of the ability you may want to require that it have to be used in an area that has already has aether present. Give a burg description of what the gist of the embed dies before the roll results, it will help tighten it up. And cleaning could reallly benefit from being listed as a confition and fleshed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1064,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","user":"miss_minty","date":". 12-21-2014, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T20:31:00-08:00","id":347131,"title":"","content":"I like your dramatic failure result, it's more creative than &quot;Make a compromise roll.&quot; The player gets a choice: take the penalty or spend Aether (a precious resource that brings its own problems) or take a hit to an important skill. I recommend explicitly stating the penalty only lasts through the scene, or make it a condition.<br /> <br /> Some concerns:<br /> Most embeds, especially informational ones, have specific, consistent outputs: a target's greatest fear or desire, the original layout of a building, or the most recent change a scene has undergone. To the best of my knowledge, there are no embeds that allow the player to ask open ended question. you have the stipulation that it won't reveal plot sensitive information is difficult to adjudicate in gameplay, rising too much or too little information, and also risks metagaming (&quot;the Storyteller just refused to answer a question, we're on the right track&quot;).<br /> <br /> Secondly, this lacks a bit of the flavor that comes with Embeds. The intent is clear, but it feels feels more like a Mage's Rote or a Vampire's Auspex effect. An embed needs to feel that is information tool once used by servants of the G-M, now re-purposed as a tool of espionage by demons.<br /> <br /> Spoofing is demonic ability, other splats might be innately immune, but they don't shouldn't need to spend any essence, quintessence, glamor, etc. If you want they can apply their supernatural potency as a penalty to the original Wits + Investigation.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the post!<br /> <br /> PS: N\u00f3 l\u00e0 minh b\u1ea1ch r\u1eb1ng b\u1ea1n l\u00e0 m\u1ed9t thi\u00ean th\u1ea7n trung th\u00e0nh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T21:18:26-08:00","id":347148,"title":"","content":"*cackles slightly* Why yes indeed, while in service I was rather loyal to the machine which I now hide from. Key word, was. When I fell, my choice was rather simple as a Destroyer. I ripped the integrator's body to shreds, letting his blood rain on a young child that he was using as a shield from me. I then took a rather intriguing book from the desk near him, and walked away to find more books like it. Since then, I have been dreaming of the day... where I can rip another integrator to pieces... or an angel. Then devour them, bit by tiny bit. Maybe a nice stew with carrots and potatoes. Sounds delicious.<br /> <br /> Anyway, me and the odd voice have been discussing the Condition &quot;Clogged&quot;, which is fixed by &quot;Cleaning&quot;, but sadly the finals the humans take every year around this time has the poor man in a tizzy over it. So it's been primarily up to me to figure out the system of it. Rather simple really.<br /> <br /> Most of the ideas have come from him, and to make note that I should have... it has yet to be thoroughly tested in play. Was going to use it, but I am rather guarded about the secrets of how it works from other people in my universe, so I want to be careful with its use. It's not something all angels have had used, it's more of a special embed that was created after the fall. Or so that's how we're wording it, but I do see the point of making it sound more along the lines of a tool. Think of it as, Sherlock Holmes Sense cranked up with Primum.<br /> <br /> When it comes to plot sensitive information, it should be worded more as &quot;You are unable to see specific details; such as Who did the crime, where are they now, etc.&quot; Again, it has yet to be used in play, but a unique opportunity to hunt down integrators has shown itself, and it can be properly tested. Any new wording shall be updated as it goes along. And with that, the roll to use it is now; Wits+Investigation-Supernatural Resistance.<br /> <br /> I would like to thank the demons of the multiverse for their generous feedback, and please keep it coming. Multiple demons giving their feed on it will make it a great asset to my arsenal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4565-zeriqharuk","name":"ZeriqHaruk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}